{"step_index":1572,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T07:33:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-13T14:33:25+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-13T14:33:27+07:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nChapter\r\nI\r\nAN UNEXPECTED PARTY\r\nIn a hole in the ground there lived a hobbit. Not a nasty, dirty, wet hole, filled with the ends of worms and an oozy smell,\r\nnor yet a dry, bare, sandy hole with nothing in it to sit down on or to eat: it was a hobbit-hole, and that means comfort.\r\nIt had a perfectly round door like a porthole, painted green, with a shiny yellow brass knob in the exact middle. The door\r\nopened on to a tube-shaped hall like a tunnel: a very comfortable tunnel without smoke, with panelled walls, and floors tiled\r\nand carpeted, provided with polished chairs, and lots and lots of pegs for hats and coats—the hobbit was fond of visitors.\r\nThe tunnel wound on and on, going fairly but not quite straight into the side of the hill—The Hill, as all the people for\r\nmany miles round called it—and many little round doors opened out of it, first on one side and then on another. No going upstairs\r\nfor the hobbit: bedrooms, bathrooms, cellars, pantries (lots of these), wardrobes (he had whole rooms devoted to clothes),\r\nkitchens, dining-rooms, all were on the same floor, and indeed on the same passage. The best rooms were all on the left-hand\r\nside (going in), for these were the only ones to have windows, deep-set round windows looking over his garden, and meadows\r\nbeyond, sloping down to the river.\r\nThis hobbit was a very well-to-do hobbit, and his name was Baggins. The Bagginses had lived in the neighbourhood of The Hill\r\nfor time out of mind, and people considered them very respectable, not only because most of them were rich, but also because\r\nthey never had any adventures or did anything unexpected: you could tell what a Baggins would say on any question without\r\nthe bother of asking him. This is a story of how a Baggins had an adventure, and found himself doing and saying things altogether\r\nunexpected. He may have lost the neighbours’ respect, but he gained—well, you will see whether he gained anything in the end.\r\nThe mother of our particular hobbit—what is a hobbit? I suppose hobbits need some description nowadays, since they have become\r\nrare and shy of the Big People, as they call us. They are (or were) a little people, about half our height, and smaller than\r\nhelps them to disappear quietly and quickly when large stupid folk like you and me come blundering along, making a noise like\r\nelephants which they can hear a mile off. They are inclined to be fat in the stomach; they dress in bright colours (chiefly\r\ngreen and yellow); wear no shoes, because their feet grow natural leathery soles and thick warm brown hair like the stuff\r\non their heads (which is curly); have long clever brown fingers, good-natured faces, and laugh deep fruity laughs (especially\r\n"}
{"step_index":1573,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T07:33:27Z","input_tokens":5306,"cache_read_tokens":85309,"output_tokens":1283,"content":"**Bisa banget!** Novel legendaris ini justru bakal makin hidup, segar, dan seru kalau dirombak pakai gaya khas lu.\n\nDi dalam file EPUB The Hobbit tersebut ada **19 Bab** lengkap serta **23 ilustrasi dan peta asli karya J.R.R. Tolkien** (*Thror’s Map, The Trolls, The Mountain-path, Mirkwood, Beorn, Smaug*, dll) yang siap diselipkan persis di sela adegan ceritanya.\n\n---\n\n### 🎨 Penerapan \"Gaya Lu\" untuk The Hobbit:\n1. **Tone Bahasa Gaul / Luwes (ID-Direct)**:\n   - Narasi luwes, tidak kaku atau harfiah seperti kamus terjemahan lama.\n   - Dinamika percakapan santai (gaya *gue/lu* atau percakapan sehari-hari yang ekspresif).\n   - Format dialog jelas dengan nama pembicara:\n     > `Gandalf: \"Selamat pagi!\"`  \n     > `Bilbo: \"Maksud lu apa? Lu doain pagi gue cerah, atau mau bilang pagi ini emang cerah terserah gue mau atau nggak...?\"`\n2. **Penjelasan Istilah Asing / Konsep Dunia Cerita**:\n   - Format konsisten: `Istilah (penjelasan sederhana)` langsung di teks secara alami tanpa merusak alur.\n   - Contoh:\n     - *Hobbit* (ras makhluk bertubuh setengah manusia dengan telapak kaki tebal berbulu lebat yang hobi rebahan nyaman dan anti-ribet).\n     - *Dwarves* (ras kurcaci kekar ahli tambang dan pandai besi yang keras kepala).\n     - *Smaug* (naga merah raksasa rakus yang merampas gunung harta kaum kurcaci).\n3. **Ilustrasi & Peta Asli Terselip Rapi**:\n   - 23 berkas peta dan sketsa hitam-putih Tolkien disematkan di momen cerita yang tepat.\n4. **Output EPUB Modern**:\n   - Dilengkapi CSS tipografi modern, daftar isi EPUB 3/2, dan kompatibel untuk semua aplikasi baca di HP/tablet/e-reader.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Contoh Preview Chapter 1 (Gaya Lu):\n\n> Di dalam sebuah lubang di dalam tanah, hiduplah seorang **Hobbit** (ras makhluk mungil bertelapak kaki tebal berbulu lebat yang hobi rebahan dan anti-petualangan).\n> \n> Bukan lubang kotor, becek, penuh cacing berlendir dan bau apek. Bukan juga lubang pasir tandus gersang yang nggak ada tempat buat duduk atau makan. Ini lubang hobbit, alias definisi kenyamanan hakiki.\n> \n> Pintunya bulat sempurna mirip *porthole* (jendela bundar di kabin kapal), dicat hijau mengilap dengan kenop kuningan kuning menyala persis di tengah. Begitu pintu dibuka, lu langsung disambut lorong berbentuk tabung mirip terowongan—terowongan super cozy tanpa asap, dinding berpanel kayu rapi, lantai berkarpet empuk, lengkap dengan deretan kursi poles dan gantungan jaket bertumpuk-tumpuk. Tuan rumah yang tinggal di sini emang paling demen nerima tamu santai.\n> \n> Nama hobbit tajir melintir ini adalah Bilbo Baggins...\n\n---\n\nGimana, mau langsung **kita gas terjemahkan dan susun jadi EPUB berilustrasi lengkap**?","thinking":"Here's the approach: adapting the source material to a casual, colloquial Indonesian style. This involves translating character traits (e.g., Bilbo's laid-back nature, Gandalf's eccentricities, the dwarves' rowdy behavior) into a relatable conversational tone. The format will use direct dialogue tags to capture the interaction style.\n\n\n"}
