{"step_index":1585,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T07:41:52Z","input_tokens":92745,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1844,"content":"Untuk novel *The Hobbit*, karena buku ini masih berstatus hak cipta, gue nggak bisa menerjemahkan teks lengkapnya secara kata-per-kata atau baris-per-baris dari awal sampai akhir. \n\nNamun, kita tetap bisa membedah dan menikmati petualangan Bilbo lewat **ringkasan cerita per bab yang santai, ulasan lore dunia Middle-earth, dan penjelasan konsep-konsep pentingnya** dengan gaya khas yang asyik dan mudah dipahami.\n\nBerikut adalah gambaran besar peristiwa di **Bab 1**:\n\n> **Bab 1: An Unexpected Party**  \n> Kehidupan tenang dan nyaman Bilbo Baggins di liang hobbit-nya mendadak buyar ketika penyihir Gandalf tiba-tiba datang dan menawarinya ikut dalam sebuah perjalanan besar. Awalnya Bilbo menolak mentah-mentah, namun keesokan harinya rumahnya justru kedatangan tiga belas kurcaci yang dipimpin oleh Thorin Oakenshield untuk berpesta dan rapat dadakan.  \n> \n> Mereka membeberkan rencana ekspedisi berbahaya untuk merebut kembali takhta serta timbunan harta karun leluhur mereka di Gunung Sunyi yang telah lama dirampas oleh naga Smaug, sekaligus menunjuk Bilbo sebagai ahli penyusup dalam misi tersebut. Meski sempat panik dan ragu, secercah rasa ingin tahu dan keberanian dalam diri Bilbo akhirnya mulai terusik.\n\nApakah lu mau lanjut melihat ringkasan santai untuk **Bab 2**?","thinking":"Copyright restrictions are paramount. The task requires summarizing or analyzing copyrighted material rather than directly quoting or translating it. Careful attention must be paid to avoid verbatim outputs or syntactic variations that would infringe on copyright.\n\n\nFocusing on general summarization, it's crucial to avoid any verbatim content or line-by-line analysis of copyrighted material. Summaries should be broad, covering substantial segments without specific references, ensuring no direct quotes or near-quotes. Direct recitation is permissible only for public domain works, direct transcriptions of user-provided media, general conversational phrases, or text already present in the conversation history.\n\n\nThe initial assumption that *The Hobbit* might be in the public domain was incorrect; copyright restrictions still apply due to the author's death date and publication year. The request for translation falls under the directive's prohibition of translations of copyrighted texts of significant length. The appropriate response involves a natural refusal, redirection to a permitted activity such as summarizing, and an offer to summarize the next segment of text.\n\n\nCannot produce a line-by-line translation of *The Hobbit* due to copyright restrictions. The response must naturally explain this, avoid direct references to system constraints, and suggest an alternative approach. Summarization of reasonably large segments, such as chapters, is permitted. A non-specific, concise style should be employed, avoiding any verbatim content or line-by-line recitation.\n\n\n"}
